    "q-36918": {
      "dom_id": "step-q36918",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given $f(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{xyz}$, find $∇f(x,y,z).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{xyz}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{xyz}}\\cdot (yz) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{xyz}}{2x} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{xyz}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{xyz}}\\cdot (xz) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{xyz}}{2y} \\\\ {f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\sqrt{xyz}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{xyz}}\\cdot (xy) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{xyz}}{2z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\text{ }i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{xyz}}{2x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{\\sqrt{xyz}}{2y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{\\sqrt{xyz}}{2z}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{xyz}}{2}(\\frac{1}{x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{z}\\text{ }k)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
